                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1741-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Lauten Audio LA-320</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Lauten Audio LA-320 is a large-diaphragm tube condenser mic from Lauten&#8217;s entry-level &#8220;Series Black&#8221; line, which incorporates the LA-120 and LA-220. All Series Black microphones are made in China.</p><p>The mic&#8217;s capsule is a K67 style, presumably 32mm O.D., and likely metallized on only one side as is common to Cardioid-only microphones. </p><p>The tube is a Chinese made 12AX7. The circuit uses an output transformer.</p><p>The LA-320 has both low- and high-cut filters, which is unique among mics in this price range. The filters are independently switchable from the front of the microphone and operate at 120Hz and 12kHz respectively.</p><p>The microphone comes with power supply, 5-pin cable, and spider shock mount all packed inside a padded briefcase.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Lauten/LA-320">Lauten Audio LA-320</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2017.</p>
